      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:14:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this branch loses the userfaultfd handling: it calls `__get_user_pages()` directly, so `FOLL_UNLOCKABLE` is never set (only `is_valid_gup_args()` adds it), `faultin_page()` doesn\u0027t pass `FAULT_FLAG_ALLOW_RETRY`, and `handle_userfault()` returns `VM_FAULT_SIGBUS`. After aosp/4367612, an O_DIRECT read into a uffd-registered range of a 4KB process would fail with `-EFAULT`.\n\naosp/4312497 fixed the same problem in `p3s_get_user_slice_pages()` by passing `\u0026locked` to `pin_user_pages_remote()` and retrying when a fault drops `mmap_lock` (it also uses `mmap_read_lock_killable()`). Could this branch do the same, or go through `__get_user_pages_locked()`, and skip the final `mmap_read_unlock()` when the lock was dropped?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "8d636ac624a6a7addcd16547a830d98e005e9f85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d1eb3f6_c33005b8",
        "filename": "mm/gup_p3s.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 86,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:14:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the spans after the first one keep the in-page offset of `start`: `__get_user_pages()` advances `start` by `PAGE_SIZE` without aligning it, `follow_page_pte()` adds `address \u0026 (mm_pte_size(mm) - 1)` for every page, and this loop only resets `offset` for native mms.\n\nFor example, `start \u003d base + 17` over two 4KB pages gives `spans[1] \u003d { slice * 4096 + 17, 17 }`, while `check_range()` in aosp/4367986 expects the start of the slice. With a middle page, `offset + length` runs into the next slice, or past the 16KB page for slice 3, where the `VM_WARN_ON_ONCE()` below fires.\n\niov_iter clamps to one page, so aosp/4367612 isn\u0027t affected, but multi-page callers of the exported API are. Would it work to record only the slice start in `follow_page_pte()` and add `in_page` in this loop for compat mms too?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "8d636ac624a6a7addcd16547a830d98e005e9f85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
